WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
This video is sponsored by Brilliant dot org.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.880
The Star Wars saga currently consists of eight films:

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.320
The original trilogy,

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.880
the ones the memes come from,

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.120
Les Mis in space,

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.120
and A New Hope 2: Electric Boogaloo.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.240
Within these films, we're introduced to 28 planets and moons

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.100
ranging from the plains of Naboo to the deserts of Tatooine to the lava of Mustafar

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.340
to the whatever this is of Felucia.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.340
A lot of these planets are clearly inspired by biomes on Earth, such as

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.020
the grasslands of Europe, the Sahara
Desert, and the lava of Hawaii.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:33.740
But scaling up one part of the Earth to a
whole planet doesn't always work within the laws of physics.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.120
A lot of the planets that we see in Star Wars could

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.960
exist in the real universe though, and we
actually have observations of similar

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.160
planets around other stars a little
closer to home. But yes, some of them are

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.440
definitely in the realm of science
fiction.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.060
That's the voice of Dr. Hannah Wakeford,

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.440
an exoplanet researcher at the Space Telescope Science Institute.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.520
With her knowledge of planetary science, my knowledge of atmospheric physics, and the

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.520
Star Wars Wikipedia which is called
Wookieepedia because of course it is

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.380
We can work out which planets in the Star Wars universe could really exist.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.380
May the Force be with us.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.660
To begin with several planets almost
identical to the Earth having lots of

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:14.480
different biomes, polar caps, and a
planetary radius of about 6400km.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.640
So Naboo, Takodana, Alderaan,
Cato Neimoidia, and Wobani can

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.060
definitely exist.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.020
Two more planets which
are very similar to the earth are Yavin 4,

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.580
the location of the rebel base in A
New Hope, and Kashyyyk, the homeworld of the wookiees.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.000
But could they exist?

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.660
C3PO: Don't be so sure.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:37.400
Yavin 4 is a large moon not much smaller than the Earth orbiting the humongous gas
giant Yavin.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.520
Yavin is so big that it's either really low density,

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.920
which would have to be caused by some strong internal heating,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.240
or it's on the very edge of what
we would even call a planet.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.720
We know that brown dwarfs, which are massive objects that are bigger than planets but not

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.340
quite massive enough to turn into stars,
can orbit other stars,

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.820
and we also know that brown dwarfs can host planets.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.200
So the existence of the moon in itself isn't impossible.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.680
The issue here is that orbiting so close to Yavin would cause

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.580
humongous amounts of tidal heating.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.260
This is the effect of the near side of the

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:14.260
moon feeling a greater gravitational
pull to the planet than the far side.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.850
In addition to this Yavin has several other
moons which are similar in size to Yavin 4

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:22.840
which would pull on the moon outwards
when nearby.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:27.020
The combination of these two factors would cause major frictional heating of the moon's interior

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.440
which would cause the moon to be extremely geologically active.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:34.380
This is exactly what we see on Io, the fifth known moon of Jupiter.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:39.610
It has over 400 active volcanoes and is
the most geologically active place in

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.160
the entire solar system.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.500
Yavin 4 isn't shown to have any volcanic activity

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.310
and though its wiki page suggests that it experienced some in the

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:53.340
past this should continue as the effects
of tidal heating will not diminish over time.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.920
So Yavin 4 as it is shown in the
movies could not exist so close to such

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.720
a large planet.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.640
Ki-Adi-Mundi: What about the droid attack on the Wookiees?

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.760
Kashyyyk

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.680
Wookiees: [roaring]

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.400
Yes, thank you.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.560
Is described as having a perfectly circular orbit,

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.360
meaning it stays the same constant
distance from its star and also has no

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.500
axial tilt, the angle between the planet's
rotation and its orbit around the star.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.180
These two combined result in the planet

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.380
having one continuous season as all parts of the planet receive constant solar heating year-round.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:27.520
There are two planets in the solar system which actually exhibit these two characteristics:

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:32.440
Mercury has almost no axial tilt and Venus has an almost perfectly circular orbit.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.800
So while it's possible that these

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.250
two characteristics could coincide and
they would indeed produce a lack of

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:41.900
seasons this would be very unlikely so
Kashyyyk gets a maybe. several other

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.300
Chewbacca: [sad grunt]

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.040
Several other Star Wars planets are also similar to what we see in the solar system

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:53.300
Tatooine for example is a combination of
Mars' dry climate with Earth's thicker atmosphere.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.580
Jakku, Jedha, and Geonosis are
also very similar, particularly Jakku

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.480
as it once had water which has since frozen
or been lost which is exactly what we

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.320
currently think happened on Mars.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.320
The interesting thing about Tatooine is that

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:09.840
it's in a binary star system: a planet
orbiting two stars which orbit each other.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.420
This gives it its famous twin
sunsets. Binary stars are in fact the

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.080
most numerous, certainly in our galaxy,
and binary stars have been observed to

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.190
have planets around them - the first
discovered was called Kepler 16b, which

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:27.110
much like Tatooine orbited two stars,
one yellow and one red, but you can have

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:32.690
many types of binary systems. Tatooine is
likely in what is called a p-type binary

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:36.890
orbit where it goes around both of the
stars, but you can also get S type

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:40.790
binaries where the planet orbits one of
the stars but not the other.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:45.980
But you would still often see two suns in the sky in both of these configurations.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:49.760
This also applies to another planet with two suns: Endor, the home of the Ewoks.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.120
Wicket: Yub Yub.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:56.720
So Tatooine, Jakku, Jedha, Geonosis, and
Endor can all exist. But there's one more

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.700
planet which is very similar to a planet
in our solar system.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.120
Bespin. It's pretty far but I think we can make it.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.360
A mining colony?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:12.060
Bespin is a gas giant, about the size of Saturn, where a cloud city floats in a breathable layer of the atmosphere.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:15.920
From the gas giants in our solar system it's very clear that it's not plausible

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.040
for a breathable stratified layer to exist in the planet's

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.140
upper atmosphere where cloud city is.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.920
If we move the gas giant close enough to

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:27.630
star we might be able to get some upper
parts of the atmosphere hot enough that

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:31.020
everything would not freeze but that's
just the first challenge.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:36.000
Say we have the right temperature at the right pressure in the atmosphere where human lungs could survive.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:41.440
Next we have to have the material to form breathable air and we have to keep it there.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.540
The air we breathe is mostly molecular nitrogen and oxygen

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.700
If we combine this in the 80/20
ratio of the Earth's atmosphere this

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:52.320
would have a mass around 12 times that
of hydrogen and helium which would be

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:55.940
making up the majority of the gas in a
gas giant planet.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:06:01.220
If the atmosphere is then stratified into layers this layer would be much much deeper in the

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:05.160
atmosphere (it's much heavier) where the
pressures would be far too high for

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.180
humans to survive and temperatures would
be much hotter too.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.800
So sadly, Bespin doesn't make the cut.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.480
Lando: It's not my fault!

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.380
This still leaves us with plenty of planets though, some of which have parallels

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:21.300
in the Earth's past, or in its future. The frozen planet of Hoth, for example,

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:25.040
is what the Earth is hypothesized to have looked like several times in its past

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.410
during periods known
as Snowball Earth. During the last of

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:32.310
these hypothesized episodes about 650
million years ago, atmospheric oxygen

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:35.790
would have been at a level which was
breathable - so Hoth as it's shown in the

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:40.920
films has historical precedent. Mustafar
by contrast is an extremely volcanically

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.660
active moon which is covered in lava
flows and active volcanoes.

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:48.140
This resembles another period in the Earth's history: 
the Hadean

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:55.020
The Hadean was an epoch about 4 billion years ago when conditions on the Earth were literally hellish.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:59.130
Extremely hot, with molten rocks
covering the surface and the planet

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:03.930
being hit by a huge number of meteorites.
The difference between the Hadean Earth

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:08.250
and Mustafar, however, is that while
Anakin and Obi-Wan are able to breathe

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:12.720
perfectly normally on Mustafar, the
atmosphere of Earth during the Hadean

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:16.280
was very dense an almost entirely carbon dioxide,

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.200
which isn't exactly breathable even to a Jedi.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:24.340
So Mustafar as shown in the movies just
doesn't really make any sense

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:27.460
Darth Vader:NOOOOOOOOOO

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:31.020
I mean, of all the people of Darth I
thought you'd be happy about that.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:35.160
Felucia is a planet that briefly
features in episode III but is

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:40.760
completely distinct from all of the
others, being a multicolored jungle of huge plants.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:43.530
The planet itself is a bit
smaller than the Earth and so has a

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:48.330
surface gravity about 75% of the Earth's -
this would help the plants to grow to

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:52.320
greater sizes, and apart from the colors
this is pretty similar to Earth during

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:57.090
the Cambrian about 500 million years ago.
So assuming the atmosphere of Felucia

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:03.460
can mix nutrients and water around the
planet with strong circulation it could exist.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.880
Two planets which resemble what
the Earth might look like in the future are

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:12.720
Coruscant and Hosnian Prime, both being densely populated planets about the same size as Earth.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.960
Coruscant is actually listed on Wookipedia as having a

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.920
population of 1 trillion beings and
judging by the cities shown in the film

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.260
this also seems about right for Hosnian Prime.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:26.020
The issue here is that Earth, with a population of just seven billion people,

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:31.240
is becoming hotter and hotter due to the buildup of gases like carbon dioxide and methane in its atmosphere.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:38.800
The effect of one trillion people on a similarly sized planet doing similar industries would be absolutely devastating.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.820
So either Coruscant and Hosnian Prime are doing some serious geoengineering

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:45.340
- not impossible given the technology in Star Wars -

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:50.100
or they should be substantially hotter than they are shown to be, so they get a maybe.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.380
Obi-Wan: I hate it when he does that

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:58.320
A planet with a similar issue is Eadu, which is shown to be covered in dense clouds and storms.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:02.300
Water vapor is actually a tremendously powerful
greenhouse gas, strongly absorbing

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:05.400
thermal wavelengths of radiation, so
assuming that Eadu is orbiting a star

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:09.680
similar to our own at a similar distance
it should actually be boiling hot.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:14.200
But it of course could be orbiting a weaker
star or further away so it could still exist.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:19.500
Two planets from the newer films
which are very similar are D'Qar and Lah'mu:

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:23.360
relatively small, terrestrial planets
which have rings similar to Saturn.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:26.900
We think of rings as being around gas
giants like Saturn and Uranus

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.190
but it's always been theoretically possible for small

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:32.680
terrestrial planets like Earth to maintain a ring system.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:38.200
And recently in October 2017 it was discovered that there's a ring system around the dwarf planet Haumea,

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.560
which orbits in our solar system just outside of Neptune.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:46.700
So it's been shown to be possible for small
terrestrial planets - even weird tiny

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:50.340
elongated ones like Haumea - to have
rings.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:55.920
There are differences between the rings though: D'Qar has rings which are composed of loose rocks,

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:59.140
consistent with a disintegrated moon or two: that could definitely exist.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:04.360
Lah'mu on the other hand looks to have rings like Saturn made of tiny ice and dust grains.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:08.800
The ice suggests that the planet formed much further out in the star system than the habitable zone

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:12.480
(the range of orbits where liquid water can exist on the surface of a planet)

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:17.020
This is kind of possible if the
habitable zone of the star moved over time

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:21.200
to allow that planet to then become
habitable, or possibly there's a very

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:24.960
strong greenhouse effect on Lah'mu, but
this still would probably impact the

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:29.560
composition of the rings that we see. So
it's a tentative maybe for Lah'mu.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:33.740
This leaves seven planets which don't have
direct analogs either in our solar system

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.780
or in the Earth's past, and...

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:40.320
Librarian: If an item does not appear in our records, 
it does not exist!

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:41.180
Sheesh.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.220
However for the past 30 years or so

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:47.820
we've observed planets around other
stars or exoplanets some of which are

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:52.000
similar to planets in our solar system
but many more are truly weird.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:57.020
There are a number of techniques we use to observe
exoplanets. The first was called radial velocity.

00:10:57.020 --> 00:11:01.340
This simply measures the pull the 
planet has on the starlight over time,

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:07.880
causing a Doppler shift in the light as it moved towards us and away from us due to the pull of its planet.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:11.800
But the most prolific method being used 
is the transit method.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:18.120
This measures the change in the amount of light seen of a star as the planet passes in front of it

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.980
and blocks out some of that light.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:24.660
From observations of thousands of exoplanets
in our region of the galaxy alone,

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.520
we know that the most common type of planets are ones we don't actually see in our own solar system:

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:34.720
Ones in between the size of our rocky earth
and the icy giants Uranus and Neptune.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:37.480
One class of planets in Star Wars are the water worlds:

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:40.200
Kamino, Ahch'To, and Scarif.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:45.500
These are planets which are almost completely covered in ocean with only small islands jutting above the water.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.860
We know that several bodies in the
solar system contain water,

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:54.780
including the moons Europa, Enceladus, and Ganymede, but only earth has liquid water on the surface

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:58.840
and while we can't directly observe 
liquid surface water on exoplanets

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:05.380
we can use other measurements as proxies, 
like the amount of water vapour in the atmosphere 
of an exoplanet.

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:10.880
Using these proxies we've discovered several objects which could potentially be ocean planets

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:17.560
such as the mini Neptune GJ 1214b.
Observations of GJ 1214b so far suggest that it's a

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:23.440
world shrouded in optically thick clouds which
would block out most of the star's light,

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:27.480
making the surface, if there is one, very
eerie and dark.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:33.280
So while we don't have direct observations of ocean planets there's nothing in planetary science that says they couldn't exist

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:35.980
and we have pretty good evidence that they should.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:39.820
So Kamino, Ahch'to, and Scarif
are quite possible.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:41.660
Lama Su: Magnificent.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:46.860
Another planet which is almost a water world is Dagobah, where Master Yoda makes his home

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:53.400
The whole planet is one massive swamp teeming with life, which implies that the planet is almost completely flat, and waterlogged.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:57.500
In fact the Wookieepedia page for Dagobah says that the planet is volcanically dead,

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:02.740
with only small remnants of any tectonic 
 activity remaining, such as the smoothed down 
remains of Mount Yoda.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:05.240
Really?

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.400
Yoda: [laughs]

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:11.800
We think of planets as being geologically
active because that's what the Earth is like:

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:16.160
constantly shifting and changing
thanks to continental drift and new land

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:22.500
being formed by volcanic action. But that
tectonic activity can just stop.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:26.880
Similar to Jakku this is what we think happened on Mars. There are plenty of features

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:31.079
such as the huge Valles Marineris and
Olympus Mons which indicate that there

00:13:31.079 --> 00:13:35.100
was tectonic activity in the past, but as
the planet cooled the molten rock

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:39.980
between the tectonic plates solidified
and the planet became volcanically dead.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:44.060
It seems like the same thing happened on
Dagobah so it could exist.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:47.760
This leaves us with three final planets 
which are truly weird:

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.960
Utapau, Mygeeto, and the invitingly named Starkiller base

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:55.180
Utapau is a really odd one.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:59.540
It's very similar to Earth in terms of the
composition and size but all the oceans

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:03.240
have drained through holes which used to
be magma chambers leaving the planet

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:07.420
barren and covered in sinkholes with
subsurface oceans

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:10.260
There are a few problems with this.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:12.750
I actually got a friend of mine with a PhD in geology to

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:17.090
look at Utapau and he sent me a
very long, angry message about how, quote

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:20.480
'geologically and physically wrong it is'

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:24.360
Firstly the water wouldn't be able to drain through holes that used to be magma chambers,

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:29.160
because magma chambers either erupt and have the rocks above them collapse, forming a caldera,

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:34.600
or as is more likely have their contents
solidify and freeze into very hard rock

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:39.060
Secondly even if all the water in the
oceans were to drain subsurface if Utapau

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:41.580
is anything like Earth then
temperatures will increase below the

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.980
surface by about 30 Celsius per
kilometer that you go down

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:48.900
So a subsurface ocean would exist either a
steam or a supercritical fluid and

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.990
because either would be less dense than
the surrounding rock it would rise to

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.240
the surface as geysers or other
geothermal activity

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.240
Which would make for a really cool planet

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:59.220
but not what we're
shown in the films

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:02.820
So in short there are a number of
problems with Utapau

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:03.980
Tion Medon: Thousands

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:08.940
Next, Mygeeto is a freezing planet similar to Hoth but the interior has completely

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:11.580
cooled and left the planet volcanically dead

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:15.000
The surface is covered with 
huge crystals of all different kinds

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:21.840
We've already seen with Hoth and Dagobah that planets can be extremely cold and can be geologically inactive,

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:25.420
so those features on Mygeeto are fine

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:30.160
The massive crystals are one of those cases where we might have to allow artistic license

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:34.200
We know that huge crystals can form 
on Earth under the right conditions

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.660
such as the cave of crystals in Mexico

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:41.700
So given exactly the right set of conditions
Mygeeto could probably exist

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:46.980
Then lastly we have Starkiller base: a planet that was hollowed out and turned into a

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:50.660
weapon that keeps the power of a star inside itself

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:52.740
In terms of the laws of physics...

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.600
Han Solo: that's not how the force works

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:56.620
Chewbacca: [I'm cold]

00:15:56.980 --> 00:16:00.180
I think we just have to give them some creative license with that one

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:03.960
So of the 28 planets and moons, 
we reckon that only five

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:08.380
couldn't exist in the real world,
with some big uncertainties on some of the others

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:12.060
But none of the worlds in
Star Wars come even close to real

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:14.660
planets we've seen around other stars

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.880
Out of the thousands of exoplanets that
have been discovered

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:20.760
none surprised people like the 
planets we now called hot Jupiters

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:25.900
They're gas giants the size of Jupiter that orbit their stars closer than mercury does to the Sun

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:28.860
and almost all orbiting in under five days

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.350
These giant planets are so close to their 
stars that they're often

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:34.880
hotter than you would be sitting under a
rocket as it took off

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.520
and that does funky things to an atmosphere

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:39.600
One such hot Jupiter has high speed winds

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:45.980
whipping around over 5000 miles an hour
with cloud droplets made of molten glass

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:51.620
Another has clouds that are likely formed
at the same substance that makes up rubies and sapphires here on Earth

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:55.080
But it's not just the giant planets that have surprised us

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:58.780
The planetary system around the star Trappist-1
has seven earth sized planets

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:02.220
orbiting it in such
a tight configuration that if life were

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:06.000
to exist there and reached our level of
technology,

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.280
planet hopping would be an easy holiday destination

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:11.730
So while science fiction might be strange,

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:16.940
it's got a long way to go before it becomes
even stranger than science fact

